    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks, that makes sense. We already tried a bit of container isolation but the issues are still cropping up. It's almost like the environment itself is shifting under us. We checked the agent logs and the network stability in the cluster seems fine, so it's not a blatant infra outage. Is there any way to track down if it's a race condition or maybe some leftover residue in the workspace that isn't getting cleared properly between runs?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To rule out leftover workspace residue, enable the strict `cleanWsDir` property in your Jenkins global settings or within job configurations to ensure a sanitized working directory for every build. Since race conditions often stem from non-deterministic sequencing, try instrumenting your test class with explicit synchronization blocks or adding a smaller, separate sleep method before critical paths to give the test more time to complete. You might also consider using a build agent with executable-only permissions to enforce that no external scripts or processes interfere with your test execution environment.",
      "source": "target",
