    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I've tried the workspace cleaning and the sleeps haven't helped much—the failures are just too random. It feels like something is actively interfering with the build process in a way we can't predictably capture in the logs. Is there any way to monitor if a side process or some rogue task is spawning and messing with the environment while the tests are actually running?",
